# Context

## Background
Outcome of the 2026-11-18 skills review (learnings.md,
notes/2026-11-18-skills-review.md). The kit had grown eight
duplicated skills/<name>/skills/<name>/ entry-point trees; five
had drifted from their top-level copies, so installs could load
whichever copy the resolver picked.

## Why This Way
Root-level SKILL.md is the documented single entry point, so the
nested trees were deleted rather than re-synced. Skill bodies now
resolve ${SKILL_DIR} at load time instead of relying on
${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}, which does not survive the flattened
layout for standalone installs.

## Gotchas
- pi-gondolin-experiments (added in db8e11e) was already flat, so
  it needed no changes here.
- marketplace.json edits only add "skills": ["."]; the catalog
  itself stays deprecated per CONTRIBUTING.md.
